      "summary": "The Monsoon session of the Indian Parliament is scheduled to commence on July 20, marking the first legislative session to be held in the newly constructed Parliament building.",
      "text": "The <strong>Monsoon session of Parliament</strong> is scheduled to commence on July 20, marking a historic transition as legislative business moves to the <mark style='background:rgba(255,210,0,0.25);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;'>new Parliament building</mark>. The session is expected to witness intense debates over key legislative agendas, including the ordinance replacing the Delhi services rules under <mark style='background:rgba(255,210,0,0.25);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;'>Article 123</mark> of the Constitution. The Cabinet Committee on Political Affairs (CCPA) recommended the dates to ensure compliance with constitutional timelines.",
